local/
.idea/
# Captured block data. Large, and a deterministic function of the seed in corpus.yml, so it is
# regenerated rather than stored: ./gradlew captureCorpus -PacceptMinecraftEula=true
#
# Everything that *describes* the corpus is committed, because terrain from a seed is the same on
# every machine: which scenarios exist, what terrain each needs, and which world they come from.
project/stonebrick/data/captures/

# Baselines stay local for now. They can be committed once the corpus is routinely regenerated from
# the seed: at that point they mean the same thing everywhere, which is what would make benchmark
# gating shareable rather than a personal habit.
project/stonebrick/baselines/
